KZ3 patch 2076 (RSX pass 72): GPU-side vertex fetch, LD_VTX_GPU=1 (default off), the RE notes "Pass 72".
The K4 walker spends ~20 of ~68 ms per frame on vertices (fetch, refs, copy, remap; rounds 69 and 71), most of it
decoding every attribute of every unique vertex into float4 slots on the CPU and uploading 16 bytes per slot.
With the switch on, a covered draw uploads the raw guest bytes its attributes span (merged per buffer) plus a
512-byte attribute table into the vertex ring, and one u32 per unique vertex (its element index); the vertex shader
decodes (root SRVs t20 = the draw's block, t21 = a decode table). The decode is written once in the C/HLSL common
subset (libs/video/rsx_vtx_gpu.h, RSX_VG_SHARED): FLOAT and HALF from the bits, UINT8/SINT16 exact conversions,
UNORM8/SNORM16/CMP32 through a table that rsx_vertex_decode_element itself fills, so the values equal the CPU path's
bit for bit (host test tools/smoke/test_vtx_gpu.sh runs the same text as C against rsx_vertex_fetch_many).
Draws with a frequency-divided or unmapped attribute, no inputs, or a block over LD_VTX_GPU_MB (8) keep the CPU
fetch; [vtx-gpu] prints both counts and the reasons per frame (mean of 60). Index buffers, refs and remap unchanged.
The GPU variant is PSO packed mode 2 (own key, one R32_UINT input); the template prewarm builds it from packed
records when the switch is on; it is never recorded. 16 failed GPU-fetch pipelines with none built turn it off.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): both (upstream branch bits before the vgpu choice; header: user-clip decl + vgpu decl).

